  "comments": [
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3c564da2_af440ca6",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1276894
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-14T16:15:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi, I am Hiro who requests this IOCTL to the Hubert\u0027s team (b/429034641).\n\nI would like to use this IOCTL in secure video playback (L1 DRM) scenario.\nThe file descriptor in REE which is allocated by restrcited dma_heap allocator is not often understood by Secure OS (e.g. OP-TEE).\nWe need to convert the file descriptor to something that the secure OS can understand.\nIt is what restricted handle is called here.\nThe design doc is attached in the description of the issue tracker too.",
      "revId": "1952cbeb1f61da8e5db3cff544dd35402ad4c57c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "895c44a3_0914e5b1",
        "filename": "include/uapi/linux/dma-heap.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 69,
      "author": {
        "id": 1945845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-14T06:09:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What is the status of this patch upstream? I feel like there have been a few restricted heap attempts.\n\nWe are usually very hesitant about adding user-visible UAPI that isn\u0027t upstream (as if something slightly different does make it upstream there can be lots of pain to make the transition).\n\nMaybe would using something other than 0x1 for the IOWR number be wise?",
      "revId": "1952cbeb1f61da8e5db3cff544dd35402ad4c57c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8f18b289_f63a70fa",
        "filename": "include/uapi/linux/dma-heap.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 69,
      "author": {
        "id": 2055842
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-14T06:48:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From the conversation with the author I think that this patch is not targeted upstream yet - indeed there are many proposals and wip implementations of the restricted heap and none is accepted by the community yet.\n\nI fully agree that in case any other implementation gets to upstream, then it would get difficult since we\u0027ll have to revert this and apply the other, or combine those two. Probably it will get much more time before any solution is worked out.\n\nAlso currently we can\u0027t see any other reasonable approach in android16-6.12 branch to handle the restricted heaps properly...",
      "parentUuid": "895c44a3_0914e5b1",
      "revId": "1952cbeb1f61da8e5db3cff544dd35402ad4c57c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e6e98d9a_08a49825",
        "filename": "include/uapi/linux/dma-heap.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 69,
      "author": {
        "id": 2055842
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-14T09:20:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Maybe would using something other than 0x1 for the IOWR number be wise?\n\nI guess that the reason behind setting this to `0x1` is just the logical order - the previous ioctl `DMA_HEAP_IOCTL_ALLOC` has value `0x0`. Is there any reason not to use `0x1`?",
      "parentUuid": "8f18b289_f63a70fa",
      "revId": "1952cbeb1f61da8e5db3cff544dd35402ad4c57c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f3992f6b_4b503c39",
        "filename": "include/uapi/linux/dma-heap.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 69,
      "author": {
        "id": 1276894
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-14T16:15:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I agree that the value doesn\u0027t have to be `0x1`. Any larger value is workable.",
      "parentUuid": "e6e98d9a_08a49825",
      "revId": "1952cbeb1f61da8e5db3cff544dd35402ad4c57c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "70ec00cb_94bce6f7",
        "filename": "include/uapi/linux/dma-heap.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 69,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-14T17:26:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We generally do not take any UAPI changes that haven\u0027t landed upstream. See https://source.android.com/docs/core/architecture/kernel/kernel-code#core-kernel-features. This becomes unsupportable if a conflicting change is made upstream.\n\nIs this needed by system code, or are the consumers of this new UAPI restricted to vendor code?",
      "parentUuid": "f3992f6b_4b503c39",
      "revId": "1952cbeb1f61da8e5db3cff544dd35402ad4c57c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "42c256b7_dfc50eda",
        "filename": "include/uapi/linux/dma-heap.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 69,
      "author": {
        "id": 2055842
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-14T17:39:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e This becomes unsupportable if a conflicting change is made upstream.\n\nAgree. I don\u0027t actaully think that this particular implementation will be sent upstream, but there is a small possibility that some inner implementation (from some third-party) of dma restricted heaps will be merged to the linux mainline and will define the API for this, as said before.\n\n\u003e Is this needed by system code, or are the consumers of this new UAPI restricted to vendor code?\n\nI\u0027m pretty sure that it will be limited to vendor code, since we plan the restricted heap implementation to be a pure vendor module.",
      "parentUuid": "70ec00cb_94bce6f7",
      "revId": "1952cbeb1f61da8e5db3cff544dd35402ad4c57c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "75a3d878_a347cdbd",
        "filename": "include/uapi/linux/dma-heap.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 69,
      "author": {
        "id": 1945845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-14T17:46:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could a separate vendor driver interface provide the same functionality here(translating a dma-buf FD to a restricted handle)?  Is there more context on why this needs to be done in the dma-buf heap interface?",
      "parentUuid": "42c256b7_dfc50eda",
      "revId": "1952cbeb1f61da8e5db3cff544dd35402ad4c57c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e9a38934_f9da5caf",
        "filename": "include/uapi/linux/dma-heap.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 69,
      "author": {
        "id": 2055842
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-14T18:17:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Theoretically, yes - although this would involve cloning (probably whole) dma_heap framework to vendor, where we can add this ioctl. That\u0027s a lot of work and we are not 100% sure that this will work as expected (not even mentioning the feasibility). Straightforward solution which guarantees that it works correctly is basically implementing a new API for this, like in the change.",
      "parentUuid": "75a3d878_a347cdbd",
      "revId": "1952cbeb1f61da8e5db3cff544dd35402ad4c57c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "78f8ad41_03cf4c6b",
        "filename": "include/uapi/linux/dma-heap.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 69,
      "author": {
        "id": 1276894
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-14T19:10:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am wondering that having a bypas node such as `/dev/dma_heap_restrcited_handle` only to get a restricted handle from secure fd and adding the ioctl for the node is easy and doesn\u0027t need UAPI and KMI change.\nBut I am not familiar with the restricted heap implementation.\nSo I would rather Friday on MediaTek answer the question.",
      "parentUuid": "e9a38934_f9da5caf",
      "revId": "1952cbeb1f61da8e5db3cff544dd35402ad4c57c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "97bce477_e38e8939",
        "filename": "include/uapi/linux/dma-heap.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 69,
      "author": {
        "id": 1945845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-14T19:20:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e this would involve cloning (probably whole) dma_heap framework to vendor, where we can add this ioctl\n\nI\u0027m not sure I see why that would be necessary.\n\nThe logic added in this patch is mostly a passthrough call to the vendor heap driver:\n```\n\tret \u003d  heap-\u003eops-\u003eget_restricted_handle(handle_data-\u003efd,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\u0026rsted_handle);\n```\n\nIt seems that the vendor heap driver could also provide a separate chardev/ioctls interface (similar to what Hiro suggested) which could do the same.",
      "parentUuid": "78f8ad41_03cf4c6b",
      "revId": "1952cbeb1f61da8e5db3cff544dd35402ad4c57c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
